        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: فخور",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "فخور — fakhūr — \"proud\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "الأم فخورة بابنها الطبيب. al-umm fakhūra bi-ibnihā aṭ-ṭabīb. The mother is proud of her son the doctor."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It takes بـ: فخور (fakhūr) بـ, proud of."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "فخور (fakhūr) is built on the native Arabic root f-kh-r, \"to boast, to glory in\" (Lane). Fakhūr is a pattern for a lasting trait: one who takes pride."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
